---
description: Keep hover/focus/active styling in shared UI primitives; do not invent per-screen interaction chrome.
globs: app/src/**/*.{tsx,ts}
alwaysApply: false
---

# Interactive states

- **Affordances** (`hover:*`, `active:*`, etc.) for buttons and controls are defined in `app/src/components/ui/button.tsx` (and other `components/ui/*` CVA modules). Do not add separate hover treatments on feature screens unless the user explicitly asks for an exception.
- In feature code, **prefer** `Button` with an existing `variant` / `size`. If a control needs a new look, add a **named variant** in the CVA (with the same neutral hover recipe as `outline` / `ghost` where appropriate: `hover:bg-muted/50`) instead of pasting utilities into the page.
- Use **`variant="bare"`** only for full-bleed hit targets (e.g. video thumbnail) or controls on custom-tinted surfaces where borders and hover must be supplied via `className`. Do not use raw `<button>` for app UI.
- Avoid conflicting utilities (e.g. `variant="outline"` plus `hover:bg-transparent`) so Tailwind’s cascade does not fight your intent.
- **Accessibility:** keep `focus-visible:ring-*` on real controls; do not remove keyboard focus styles when fixing hover.

```tsx
// ❌ Raw element — use Button from @/components/ui/button
<button type="button" className="..." />

// ✅ Default
<Button type="button" variant="outline" className="..." />

// ✅ Full-bleed thumbnail / tinted toolbar only (`bare` in button.tsx)
<Button type="button" variant="bare" className="..." />
```
